test_command=for t in tests/*_test.sh; do sh "$t" || exit 1; done
id=closingblock-01 result=green reason=unit tests "closingblock-01: the specifier/coder/verifier/orchestrator prompt's report section requires the three-line closing block, a mirror only, with the receipt as authority" (four tests, one per role) pass -- each role's report section (specifier "## Output, written to...", coder "## Output", verifier "## Report Format", orchestrator "## Report Format") now requires the report to end with a closing block of exactly three consecutive lines `status=<value>`, `ids=<id,id,...>`, `results=<value>` -- grep-able, short, deterministic -- and states the block is a mirror only: no routing, count, or decision ever derives from it, and wherever a disk receipt exists, the receipt is the authority over the block's mirrored values
id=closingblock-02 result=green reason=unit tests "closingblock-02 (specifier row)", "closingblock-02 (coder row)", "closingblock-02 (verifier row)", and "closingblock-02 (orchestrator row)" pass -- the per-role value vocabularies are pinned in the prompts: specifier status=spec_complete / the declared ids of the sub-specs it wrote / results=none; coder status done|blocked / its sub-spec's declared ids / comma-joined id=<id> result=<green|skip|blocked> tokens mirroring its receipt in receipt order; verifier status approved|rejected (approved-with-warnings folds to approved, the prose verdict stays authoritative) / the change's declared ids / tokens from the receipts as found on disk at verification end; orchestrator status delegated-specifier|delegated-coder|delegated-verifier|stopped|released|waiting-user / the ids from the probe / comma-joined <subspec-file>=<done|blocked|in_progress> per sub-spec from the probe's class fields
id=closingblock-03 result=green reason=unit tests "closingblock-03: the coder's report names its receipt file and its results= tokens match the receipt's id lines exactly (receipt is the authority, deviation absorbed by the bounded REJECTED.md retry)" and "closingblock-03: a coder session that refused before touching the sub-spec still closes honestly -- status=blocked with the BLOCKED: reason in the report prose" pass -- the coder prompt's "## Output" gains the name-the-receipt bullet (the receipt file it wrote or updated is named in the report body) and the closing-block bullet states the results= tokens must match that receipt's id lines exactly (the disk receipt is the authority; a deviation is a bug, absorbed by the bounded REJECTED.md retry) and that a refused session still closes honestly with status=blocked and the BLOCKED: reason in the report prose
id=closingblock-04 result=green reason=unit tests "closingblock-04: every role's report section states the block is never an input to any routing state or count" and "closingblock-04: AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md carry the closing-block convention byte-identically" pass -- all four report sections carry the never-an-input-to-any-routing-state-or-count wording (extending prompts-06's skills-line rule), and both policy docs carry the byte-identical "- Closing block: ..." gotcha bullet (cmp-verified) stating the three-line grammar, the per-role vocabularies, mirror only, and the receipt as authority
id=closingblock-05 result=green reason=unit tests "closingblock-05: the specifier prompt's diff vs HEAD is purely additive and every added line carries the closing-block requirement" and "closingblock-05: no existing specifier prompt line is reworded or removed (every pre-change line survives verbatim)" pass -- the specifier prompt's historical byte-for-byte pin (tests/skills-activation-prompts_test.sh prompts-05) is lifted for exactly this additive edit: the diff vs git HEAD adds only the closing-block bullet to the "## Output, written to..." section (no removed lines, every pre-change line survives verbatim), and prompts-05 is evolved to the retirement-note precedent (byte-identity enforced while unchanged; once the edit lands, a loud note plus the additive-shape guard the lifting sub-spec demands)
id=closingblock-06 result=green reason=unit tests "closingblock-06: VERSION is a semver agreeing with the newest (topmost) CHANGELOG entry -- never a pinned literal", "closingblock-06: VERSION's only content is the version value with one trailing newline", "closingblock-06: CHANGELOG.md carries the '## [4.3.0] - 2026-09-11' section above the [4.2.1] section", "closingblock-06: the [4.3.0] entry describes change 1 -- the orchestrator scripts extracted to scripts/orchestration/ with install.sh injecting them into the rendered antz-orchestrator body (no behavior change)", "closingblock-06: the [4.3.0] entry describes change 2 -- the session guards (dedup and the post-stop latch)", "closingblock-06: the [4.3.0] entry describes change 3 -- the coder-written result receipts with the orchestrator's file-reading classification and the doubtful-receipt suite exception", "closingblock-06: the [4.3.0] entry describes the closing-block convention (a mirror only)", and "closingblock-06: every CHANGELOG entry other than this change's own (the [4.2.1]-down tail) is byte-untouched versus git HEAD" pass -- VERSION reads 4.3.0 (newline-terminated only content, agreeing with the newest entry per the no-cross-change-pin lesson), the dated [4.3.0] entry sits above [4.2.1] with Added/Changed sections describing all three improvements plus the closing-block convention, and the [4.2.1]-down tail is byte-identical to git HEAD
id=closingblock-07 result=green reason=unit test "closingblock-07: the [4.3.0] entry grades minor with the versioning-table justification -- not patch (not wording-only), not major (contract/marker format/access model/directory layout/install locations unchanged, the receipt file additive)" passes -- the entry's grading paragraph states minor (change 1 alters install.sh's rendered agent bodies = a behavior change to the render; change 3 changes role behavior: the coder's receipt duty, the orchestrator's classification source), explicitly not patch (not wording-only: rendered output and role behavior change) and not major (the workflow contract, the antz:generated marker format, the access model, the directory layout, and the install locations are all unchanged -- the receipt file is additive inside the existing change directory)
